Key Takeaway

Azure Virtual Network Peering enables secure, high-performance communication between Azure Virtual Networks using Microsoft's private backbone infrastructure. By combining peering, gateway transit, user-defined routes, and service chaining, Azure Administrators can build scalable, secure, and highly available enterprise networking architectures that support both cloud-native and hybrid environments.
